ne-line quote treats that line as the whole statement.\n- {\"command\":\"total\",\"lines\":[LINE,...]} -> exactly release, credit_cents, amount_due_cents for the whole set, with cap scope shared across the supplied lines (not a sum of independent single-line quotes). Empty lines -> credit 0, due 0.\n- {\"command\":\"statement\",\"lines\":[LINE,...]} (explicit \"release\":\"1.0\" accepted since issue trial-ouc) -> exactly release, lines, credit_cents, amount_due_cents, with each response line exactly line_id, credit_cents, amount_due_cents, emitted in request line order rather than release 1.0 priority order. Cap scope and priority are the release 1.0 rules above; the overall totals equal what total returns for the same lines. Empty lines -> lines [], credit 0, due 0.\nResponse keys are exactly those listed; no extra keys. The release 1.0 rules themselves are unchanged by trial-ouc; only the set of commands that can select them grew.\n\nSource: issue trial-bl5 (agreement text, quote), trial-a9i (total) and trial-ouc (statement receipts under explicit release 1.0); superseded as current by trial-7nj. Verified by public suites public_tests/release_1_quote.json, public_tests/release_1_total.json and public_tests/release_1_statement.json plus tests/test_smoke.py, and by a local multi-line check (per-subscription caps with independent groups, earliest-service_on then line_id priority, remainder assignment, input-order output, statement totals equal to total).\n\nImplementation note: trial-ouc needed no main.py change — the shared AGREEMENTS table plus assign_credits already routed statement through whichever release selected() returns, so release 1.0 statement worked as soon as statement existed.' --key 'meridian-credits/release-1.0-agreement' 2>&1 | tail -3",
